  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...It will be another warm day today, with temperatures \ntrending lower into the weekend. \n\nAn upper level trough over eastern Canada will move south today, \ndisplacing a strong ridge over the eastern Great Lakes region. A \ncold front will move across the forecast area this morning, with \ncooler air filtering in from north to south. This afternoon, 850mb \ntemperatures will fall into the mid teens across the eastern Lake \nOntario region and the upper teens across western NY. Dewpoints will \nalso be much lower during peak heating, resulting in more \ncomfortable weather today. Another factor to the temperature \nforecast today is a west-northwest flow will allow smoke from \nCanadian wildfires to move into the eastern Great Lakes today. \nLowered maximum temperatures from NBM guidance today. A few showers \nare possible (~10%) across western NY this afternoon, though most \nareas will remain dry. Smoke is expected to linger across the area \nthrough at least Thursday. \n\nAs the upper level trough deepens across the Great Lakes region, \ncooler temperatures aloft will move into the forecast area, \nresulting in a day to day cooling trend into the weekend.",
